  "operation": {
    "name": "ChaCha block function (SSSE3 form): four blocks in parallel with feed-forward, the state's 64-bit counter advanced by 4",
    "contract": "input rdi = a state record of which bytes 0x00..0x30 are read (key rows at +0x00/+0x10 and the counter/nonce row at +0x20, whose first 64-bit word is the counter); esi = round-loop iterations (two double rounds each); output rdx receives 256 bytes -- four 64-byte ChaCha blocks for counters c, c+1, c+2, c+3, each the sum of its worked state and its initial state -- and the counter word at [rdi+0x20] is stored back advanced by 4; no return value",
    "evidence": [
      "the body's round constants are the ChaCha constants: the 16-byte ASCII string \"expand 32-byte k\" at 0x4519c0 (the sigma row) and, for the zero-round path, its exact double at 0x456c50 (per-word 2*sigma)",
      "the round loop is the ChaCha quarter-round network on 32-bit words: paddd/pxor with rotations 16 (pshuflw/pshufhw 0xb1 word swaps), 12 (psrld 0x14 / pslld 0xc), 8 (pshufb through the byte-rotation mask at 0x4531c0) and 7 (psrld 0x19 / pslld 0x7), with pshufd 0x39/0x4e/0x93 lane rotations for the diagonal rounds and a second byte mask at 0x452ec0",
      "the entry builds four counter rows from the 64-bit counter at [rdi+0x20] (+0/+1/+2/+3, carry into the high dword) -- four blocks are worked in lockstep, one counter step apart, in transposed (row-per-register) form",
      "the epilogue is the ChaCha feed-forward: worked rows are added to the entry-saved initial rows (the constant rows receive their sigma add just after the loop) and stored as 16 vector stores covering 256 bytes, and the counter row is stored back at [rdi+0x20] with the counter advanced by 4",
      "with esi == 0 the body still writes the full 256 bytes: initial + initial, the constant rows via the precomputed doubled sigma -- the esi parameter counts loop iterations, so the caller chooses the round count (each iteration is two double rounds)",
      "the set arm is the family's only tail-jump arm: the dispatcher unwinds its own frame and jumps, so the F2 body runs with the dispatcher's caller arguments and returns to that caller directly",
      "the dispatcher's clear region is the same ChaCha computation in SSE2 form (1,753 bytes, hash-verified against the #2616 pin): same sigma/doubled-sigma constants, same counter construction, same epilogue, and no pshufb anywhere -- the 8-rotation is done with psrld 0x18 / pslld 0x8 shift pairs, which is exactly the SSSE3 gap bit 9 tests"
    ]
  },
